   1          /*
   2             File: rx_ecc.c
   3             Module: Group 3  Error Correction (PESEC SEC+DED)
   4          
   5             Implementation of:
   6               - PESEC matrix construction (mirroring the TX encoder)
   7               - PESEC syndrome computation and single-bit error correction
   8               - SEC+DED overall parity check for double-error detection
   9          
  10             The earlier H1-type differential validation layer has been removed.
  11             Nibble decoding is now performed exclusively by absolute syndrome
  12             computation in rx_decoder.c::rx_process_bus_state(), which relies on
  13             the TX invariant  syndrome(current_bus_state) == last_input_nibble.
  14             PESEC alone guards the 26-bit codeword against single-bit errors
  15             (corrected) and double-bit errors (detected and dropped).
  16          
  17             SEC+DED:
  18               rx_pesec_correct() accepts an overall_parity parameter.  The TX
  19               computes P = parity(data[14:0]) XOR parity(red[9:0]) and shifts it
  20               out as the 26th bus bit.  The RX recomputes parity locally and
  21               compares it with the received P.  Combined with the PESEC
  22               syndrome, this yields a 4-case truth table:
  23          
  24                 Syndrome | Parity Check | Meaning
  25                 ---------|--------------|------------------------------------------
  26                   == 0   |     OK       | No error (PESEC_NO_ERROR)
  27                   != 0   |     FAIL     | Single error -> correct (PESEC_CORRECTED_*)
  28                   != 0   |     OK       | Double error -> uncorrectable (PESEC_UNCORRECTABLE)
  29                   == 0   |     FAIL     | Parity bit itself flipped (PESEC_CORRECTED_PARITY)
  30          
  31             Dependencies:
  32               rx_types.h    ->  uint8_t, uint16_t, constants
  33          
  34             Portability:
  35               No hardware registers are accessed here.
  36          
  37          */
